## Documentation Structure

> The commands look up files by **role**, using this table. Update the paths to match your docs.
> Leave a row out (or write `n/a`) if you don't have that doc. Commands skip roles that are missing.

| Role | Path | Purpose |
|------|------|---------|
| Index | `[path/to/index.md]` | Main navigation / overview |
| Network | `[path/to/network.md]` | VLANs, topology, DNS, remote access |
| Proxmox | `[path/to/proxmox.md]` | Nodes, VMs, LXCs, templates |
| Storage | `[path/to/storage.md]` | NAS, NFS exports, storage pools, backups |
| Kubernetes | `[path/to/kubernetes.md]` | Optional |
| Services | `[path/to/services.md]` | Service catalog (name, URL, host, port, auth) |
| IP Map | `[path/to/ip-map.md]` | Every IP allocation |
| Reverse Proxy | `[path/to/traefik.md]` | Routing conventions |
| SSO | `[path/to/sso.md]` | Authentik / Authelia setup |
| Monitoring | `[path/to/monitoring.md]` | Prometheus, Grafana, Uptime Kuma, etc. |
| Automation | `[path/to/automation.md]` | Terraform / Ansible / CI patterns |
| Onboarding | `[path/to/new-service-guide.md]` | How you add a new service |
| Troubleshooting | `[path/to/troubleshooting.md]` | Known issues and fixes |
| Runbooks | `[path/to/runbooks/]` | Where generated runbooks are saved |
| Changelog | `[path/to/Homelab Changelog.md]` | Infrastructure change log (see Change Protocol) |
| Task Registry | `[path/to/Task Registry.md]` | Agent task coordination (see Task Coordination) |
| Sensitive | `[path/to/credentials.md]` | **Never read or print.** Listed only so the agent avoids it |

Starter files for the Changelog and Task Registry are in the repo's `templates/` folder.

